# Reusable Slack Alert Workflow Runbook
## Overview

This runbook provides guidance on adding the reusable Slack alert workflow to an existing workflow

## Inputs

| Input | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `status` | The status of the job that the Slack alert depends on. Typically, this is set to `${{ needs.<job_id>.result }}`. |
| `workflow-name` | The name of the workflow. Typically, this is set to `${{ github.workflow }}`. |

| Secret | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `slack-webhook-url` | The Slack webhook URL used to send the alert. Typically, this is set to `${{ secrets.SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL }}`. |

## Example Usage

Below is an example with how the reusable Slack alert workflow can be added to an existing workflow.

```yaml
jobs:
  example-job-1:
    ...
  reusable-slack-alert:
    needs: example-job-1
    uses: ministryofjustice/ministry-of-justice-engineering-platform/.github/workflows/reusable-slack-alert.yml@96de26562471386ca5d20cc77e7dbaf7e7956311
    if: ${{ always() }} # Ensures the Slack alert runs regardless of the previous job's result
    with:
      status: ${{ needs.example-job-1.result }}
      workflow-name: ${{ github.workflow }}
    secrets:
      slack-webhook-url: ${{ secrets.SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL }}
```